what is up everybody it's animak here  for anime uproar and the mha manga just  keeps getting darker and more brutal in  this final arc the number one pro hero  is sacrificing his life right in front  of us in a battle to the death  all for one is now eating people's souls  or something and what is happening with  deku events are moving quickly the story  is intense so let's talk about it right  now  you guys know how this works if you  enjoy our videos and you want to see  more just leave a quick like and comment  it costs you nothing and it takes you  only a second but it helps us out a lot  and of course if you want to see more  videos in the future just click  subscribe and hit that bell and you're  set finally this video will contain mha  manga spoilers so please proceed with  caution you have been warned okay so  remember how two chapters ago i said in  a video that endeavour's right arm had  been ripped off by all for one and then  in my video on the previous chapter i  had to correct myself because it turned  out that endeavour's arm was fine he was  just injured in the area below his right  armpit well about that  but more on that later the latest  chapter starts off with giro tokuyami  and hawks still facing off against all  for one and all for one is still being  weakened by his own quirks rebelling  against him on the inside in the  previous chapter we saw that all for  one's mask had been partially destroyed  and in this chapter tokuyami uses an  attack with like the most emo name ever  to smash all for one in the face with  dark shadow and destroy the rest of his  mask but even with the mask destroyed  the heroes continue to attack all for  one relentlessly hawks proclaims that  they are not just trying to buy time  until endeavour recovers and is able to  join the fight again despite the fact  that they are not as strong as endeavor  hawks tokyami and jiro are going all out  and they're doing their best to defeat  all for one before he can do any more  damage for his part all for one is  surprised that he wasn't able to easily  dodge these attacks even after losing  his hearing and eyesight to the severe  injuries he sustained during his first  battle with all might he still had  superior senses to normal humans because  he was able to use multiple sensory  quirks including infrared vision  detecting vibrations and so on but now  all of these quirks that he relied on  are rebelling against him from the  inside and this is really slowing him  down and making him weaker in this  crucial moment also this has never  happened to of one before and he still  hasn't figured out why exactly these  consciousnesses or vestiges inside of  him which he refers to as fragile  reproductions are able to fight back  against him all for one then proceeds to  attack the rebellious quirks inside of  him and he appears to be eating the  vestiges almost like he is devouring the  souls of the former users he looks like  he's about to eat the white-haired woman  that we saw in the previous chapter and  then before hawks can deliver the  finishing blow an explosion of rivet  stabs emerges from all for one's body  the rivets are able to protect all for  one while injuring hawks and they also  seem to be repairing all for one's mask  by gathering up all the broken pieces  and putting them back together at least  that's what it looked like to me based  on the panels for a moment it appears as  if hawks tokyoami and jiro are about to  be turned into swiss cheese by all these  rivets but that is when endeavour  arrives to save the day he puts his own  body between hawks and the rivets and he  begins smashing the rivets with his  fists however some of the rivets pierce  through his right hand and eventually  his right arm is torn off just above the  elbow as a fierce and furious endeavor  rushes at all for one so yeah if anyone  tells you that i was wrong about  endeavour getting his right arm ripped  off two chapters ago you can tell him  that i wasn't wrong i was just using  future sight the chapter then gives us a  break from all that insane action in  order to reveal some of endeavour's  backstory including the story of how he  really decided to become the hero he is  today back when ng todoroki was a boy  around high school age he witnessed a  father desperately trying to save his  daughter from a villain but the father  failed and both he and the daughter were  brutally killed by the villain right in  front of angie in that moment angie  understood firsthand just how much  better all might is compared to ordinary  people almight was out there fighting  villains like this every single day and  yet for an ordinary human one wrong move  and they could be killed in an instant  angie felt intense feelings of  inferiority and even jealousy towards  all might in this moment and that's when  he decided to make his hero name  endeavor the name represents angie's  determination to work hard and keep  striving until he one day surpasses even  almight himself and in this moment back  in the present time endeavour finally  realizes the truth he will never be like  all might or deku and he was never  really fighting to surpass all might  anyway all this time endeavor has been  fighting against himself against his own  weakness and sense of powerlessness  when he witnessed the death of that  father and daughter at the hands of a  villain he felt weak and powerless and  all this time he has been fighting to  escape that feeling he has been fighting  to outrun his own weakness  his giant ego his obsession with all  might his abusive behavior towards shoto  and the rest of his family none of that  was really about becoming the number one  pro hero or about becoming the strongest  for his entire life endeavor has been  driven by his sense of weakness and his  desperate desire to overcome it it is  not the pursuit of strength in itself  that he has been living for but the fear  of his own weakness  and now finally endeavour seems to  understand instead of cursing his  weakness he embraces it and he launches  an all-out attack at all for one he uses  his quirk to generate a new hand made of  flames in the place of his old one and  he unleashes the full force of his  attack into all for one's body as all  for one falls back under the force of  endeavors flames angie todoroki declares  that ending this fight once and for all  is his duty and that is how this chapter  ends  wow we are witnessing such incredible  character progression from endeavor when  he was first introduced in the story he  came off as this narcissistic egomaniac  who just wanted to become the strongest  hero in the world in order to satisfy  his own petty ego and yet  that was only scratching the surface of  his character we now know that  endeavour's obsession with becoming the  strongest and surpassing all might  didn't come from just a petty desire to  be the best instead it came from a  deeply ingrained childhood trauma angie  witnessed a horrific crime and he felt  powerless to do anything as two people  were brutally slain right in front of  him that feeling of weakness and  helplessness horrified him and he never  wanted to feel that way again  so he got it into his head that he had  to become the number one pro hero and  that he had to surpass all might at all  costs but not so that he could brag  about it and bask in his own glory angie  felt that he had to do this just so he  could stop being afraid and he thought  that the only way to overcome his  feelings of fear and inadequacy was to  become the strongest or to raise his son  to become the strongest if we look deep  enough beneath the surface we realized  that angie didn't do what he did because  he was cocky or competitive in reality  he did it because he was scared and  becoming the strongest was the only way  for angie to convince himself that he  doesn't need to be afraid anymore now  none of that excuses the bad things that  he willingly chose to do but this does  tell us where it all started and how  angie became the man he is today i  honestly think that endeavor is the best  written character in mha at this point  in time he is a deeply flawed  multifaceted character and he just feels  like a fully fleshed out imperfect human  being honestly kudos to horikoshi for  giving this man a phenomenal character  arc drop me a line down in the comments  with your thoughts on endeavour's  character do you agree with me that he  is the best written character in the  story or do you just hate him because of  the bad things he's done in the past we  also need to talk about all for one's  apparent ability to just like consume  the vestiges that were rebelling against  him i mean is it really going to be that  easy after placing all of that emphasis  on the fact that something like this has  never happened to all for one before is  horikoshi really just gonna be like okay  he's back to normal now he just ate the  souls of the other users no big deal  honestly i'm not sure what's gonna  happen but i do feel that that  white-haired woman may end up being  important in the future i could be  totally wrong on this but we'll have to  wait and see nevertheless if all for one  really can somehow consume the vestiges  and neutralize them completely then we  have to think about the massive  implications that this could have for  deku and one for all i mean what if all  for one finds a way to consume the  vestiges of one for all which would  neutralize them and clear the way for  one for all to finally be stolen all for  one defeating his own rebellious  vestiges was just like a quick creepy  scene but we can't underestimate the  potentially massive consequences of this  reveal for the final battle between  shigaraki and deku definitely let me  know what you guys thought of this and  do you think that all for one consuming  the vestiges foreshadows the possibility  of all for one consuming the vestiges  within one for all also why haven't we  seen deku in almost three months i think  the last time we saw him was chapter 349  so like seven chapters ago  with this being the final arc and  everything you would think that the main  character would get more screen time i  know a lot of people have been saying  that horikoshi is rushing the mha manga  but i really don't think that's true  if he was rushing then he could have  just gone right to the main battle  between deku and shigaraki and  everything else could have just been  shown in quick bursts during that final  battle or it could even happen  off-screen the way that horikoshi is  structuring this war arc and the way he  has sidelined deku over the past few  months tells me that he isn't really  rushing he is clearly moving at the pace  he's comfortable with and he's taking  his time with the side battles before  getting to the main event do you guys  agree let me know down below as always  if you enjoyed the video and you want to  see more in the future leave a quick  like and comment it only takes you a  second but it helps me out a lot and of  course subscribing and hitting that bell  is a completely free way of directly  supporting this channel you can also hit  me up on twitter and instagram at  animeopror i want to give a big thank  you to all of our anime outpour patrons  for making videos like this one possible  special thank you to kyle salisbury this  man is an absolute mad lad and a  disciple of lord twigo himself and i  can't forget all of our the one tier  patrons the ones who rise above all  other clans including alpha sigma pate  heffa the red-haired fox hinokami and  water the toasted chi corey mcgowan the  fallen chosen orihime wukong dante  tinnell and big buddhist finally thank  you also to our pro hero tier patrons  including the one and only gilgamesh on  hell cruz alicia octor bonnie parks fat  boy games kaido might be a duck alivania  and anime s codem if you guys enjoy our  videos and you feel that they provide